  "published": "2026-07-27T08:05:53.887Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Adds CC036: flags blocking System.Net.Sockets.Socket operations (Receive, Send, Accept, Connect and friends) inside async code. A socket call parks a thread-pool thread until the network responds, or a TCP timeout that can run into minutes; Accept and Connect can block indefinitely. Separate from CC028 because Socket's async counterparts are not signature-compatible — Receive(byte[]) pairs with ReceiveAsync(Memory<byte>, CancellationToken) — and that compatibility is what makes CC028's rewrites safe; NetworkStream remains covered by CC028. Analyzer-only. 36 diagnostics.",
